{"entities":[{"pmid":"8599504","text":"Angioedema","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D000799","start":0,"end":10},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"droperidol","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D004329","start":27,"end":37},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"Angioedema","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D000799","start":54,"end":64},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"angioneurotic edema","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D000799","start":80,"end":99},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"Quincke's disease","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D000799","start":103,"end":120},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"edema","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D004487","start":154,"end":159},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"upper-airway obstruction","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D000402","start":210,"end":234},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"drug allergies","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D004342","start":309,"end":323},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"angioedema","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D000799","start":332,"end":342},{"pmid":"8599504","text":"droperidol","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D004329","start":464,"end":474}],"gold_relations":"droperidol | CID | angioedema","metrics":{"precision":0.5,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.6666666666666666,"tp":1,"fp":1,"fn":0,"rel_precision":0.5,"rel_recall":1.0,"rel_f1":0.6666666666666666,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":1,"rel_fn":0},"pmid":"8599504","relations":["D004329 | CID | D014060","D004329 | CID | D000799"],"text":"Angioedema associated with droperidol administration. Angioedema, also known as angioneurotic edema or Quincke's disease, is a well-demarcated, localized edema involving the subcutaneous tissues that may cause upper-airway obstruction. We report the case of a previously healthy 19-year-old man with no known drug allergies in whom angioedema with significant tongue swelling and protrusion developed within 10 minutes of the administration of a single IV dose of droperidol."}